# One line ending everywhere.
#
# The repository is worked on from Windows, where Git's default `autocrlf`
# rewrites files to CRLF on checkout. Prettier is configured for LF, so files
# touched on Windows started failing `prettier --check` for their line endings
# alone — which is noise in a diff and, once there is a format gate in CI, a
# red build for nothing.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the repository and checks LF out on
# every platform, so the working copy and the committed bytes agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
